# handoff-packet.toon — the ONE artefact that crosses the boundary between a smith and
# a reviewer (plan 203 §3). A smith writes it when it stops; a reviewer reads it before
# anything else. No packet, no review. Written in the house's TOON face so a human reads
# it and a script diffs it.
#
# RULES THIS SCHEMA ENFORCES ON ITS WRITER
#   1. head  is the commit the packet SPEAKS FOR. The reviewer fetches `branch`, and if
#      the fetched head sha differs from `head` here, the review is REFUSED. A packet that
#      does not name the tree it describes is not a packet.
#   2. gates and tests carry OUTPUT, never the name of a gate and never "all pass".
#      An empty tail is a claim of silence, and silence is not evidence.
#   3. claims[] is one line per thing the smith asserts it DID, so the reviewer can mark
#      each `verified` or `unverified`. An unverified claim is not a fault; a claim with
#      no evidence behind it is.
#   4. not_done[] names what was deliberately left, and why. An empty list is a POSITIVE
#      claim that nothing was left, and a reviewer may test it.
#   5. needs[] names what the smith could not settle alone (a decision, a key, a licence).
#      A need is not a failure; hiding one is.
#   6. A smith never fills `review` — that block belongs to the reviewer and is appended
#      only after the gates have been run on the machine that will hold the merge.
#   7. `records[]` says which of the PROJECT'S records the work touched — each path, and what
#      changed there. A packet with an empty block is refused, and `none` must carry a reason a
#      reviewer can weigh: a project's decisions, handoff, plans and boards are updated by the
#      work, or the work has not landed (plan 291 part 2, at the Allfather's word).
#
# FIELDS (see plan 203 §3 — this file is the plan, made writable)
#   packet[1]{task,plan,branch,base,head,author,written_at,ruleset,floor}
#     task        one sentence: what this was supposed to be
#     plan        the document that says so (home plan path or repo docs path)
#     branch      the smith's own branch — `eins/<id>` (the transport, never a PR)
#     base        what it was cut from: origin/main, or the `eindri/<id>` branch when the
#                 smith was cut from an UNMERGED branch (bin/forge/gather.sh merges that base first)
#     head        the 40-char sha the packet stands for — the reviewer compares it
#     author      the agent that authored it (never `brokk` — Rule 44)
#     written_at  ISO-8601 UTC
#     ruleset     the ruleset hash the smith judged itself against, or `none`
#     floor       `complete` | `partial` — a partial floor is a refusal waiting to happen
#   changed[N]{path,added,removed,why}
#   gates[N]{gate,cmd,exit,output_tail}      output_tail: last lines of real output
#   tests[N]{cmd,exit,tail}
#   claims[N]{claim,state,evidence}          state: verified | unverified (smith's own view)
#   records[N]{path,what}                    the project records touched — or one row
#                                            `none` + the reason nothing changed (never empty)
#   not_done[N]{item,why}
#   needs[N]{need,who}                       who: allfather | operator | licence | key
#   review[0..1]{reviewer,at,ruleset,gates,tests,verdict,pr,merge,commit}
#     written ONLY by the reviewer; absent until a review has actually run
#
# A packet is a PROMISE, not a proof. The proof is the reviewer's, and it is written below
# the line the smith may not cross.
packet[1]{task,plan,branch,base,head,author,written_at,ruleset,floor}:
  "<what this was supposed to be>","<plan path>","eins/<id>","origin/main","<40-hex sha>","<agent>","<ISO-8601Z>","<ruleset hash | none>","complete|partial"

changed[N]{path,added,removed,why}:
  "<path>",0,0,"<why this file is in the diff>"

gates[N]{gate,cmd,exit,output_tail}:
  "<docs|assets|csv|units|tables|baton|engine>","<the command actually run>",0,"<last lines of its output>"

tests[N]{cmd,exit,tail}:
  "<the test command actually run>",0,"<last lines>"

claims[N]{claim,state,evidence}:
  "<one line the smith asserts it did>","verified|unverified","<where the reviewer can look>"

records[N]{path,what}:
  "<a project record the work updated, or `none`>","<what changed there, or why no record changed>"

not_done[N]{item,why}:
  "<what was left>","<why it was left, never silence>"

needs[N]{need,who}:
  "<what the smith could not settle>","allfather|operator|licence|key"
